> talk to him
The beggar looks up at you with weary, cloudy eyes. "Spare a copper for a poor
soul, sir?" he rasps, shuffling his palm forward. "A bite of bread or a coin to
warm my bones, and I'd be eternally grateful." He seems too weak and distracted
by hunger to offer much conversation.

> ask him about stones
"Stones I have plenty of, master. They're free, and they don't fill a belly." He
gestures vaguely at the roadside gravel and lets his hand fall back into its
begging posture.

