the dusty road towards the village.

The Village
The village consists of a dozen timber-framed houses lining either side of the
road. Despite its modest size, the area is full of life and bustle. It is market
day.

A hawker stands behind a sturdy wooden bench by the roadside. On the surface lie
three upturned cups. The man gestures grandly over them and shouts to the crowd,
"Test your skill and win ten silver coins!"

Catching your eye, he grins wide. "Ah, my good wizard! How about trying your
luck? Stake a single silver coin and win ten times your wager!"

> talk to hawker
The hawker doesn't seem interested.

"To show my goodwill, I will let you play once for free. Now watch carefully,"
says the hawker, taking out a little stone which he places under one of the cups
on the bench. He then starts to move the cups this way and that.

