Meadow
You stand in a small, overgrown clearing dominated by a dilapidated hut hunched
immediately to the south. Looming on all other sides is a dense, ancient forest
whose twisted boughs form an impenetrable wall of shadow. A faint dirt path cuts
through the weeds, winding away north into the dark tree line.

> s
As you enter the hut your old mentor says, "I see you have found a new stone.
Well done. Put it in the gilded box."

Hut
The interior of the hut is cramped and gloomy. Thick soot cakes the solitary
window, leaving the flickering flames of a stone hearth as the room's sole
source of light. Atop the fire, rusted iron vessels bubble quietly, venting
strange, multi-coloured vapours. A massive, cluttered workbench is buried under
a chaotic heap of heavy grimoires, brittle sheets of paper, and exotic
alchemical ingredients. A heavy wooden door leads north, back out to the forest
path.

Resting within a small alcove in the stone wall is a beautifully carved, gilded
wooden box. It contains a black stone.

Your mentor ponders something.

You can also see a folio here.

> give green stone to mentor
Istar frowns slightly, lowering his voice. "The Stone of Verdure. Bound to the
